          "note": "Macro, rotating, chrome reflections off M56's synthetic environment -- the one place in the piece where the metal finish is the subject. The fugue reaches its first full cadence here, which is why the shot is short and the camera arc small: nothing should compete with the cadence. The caption is the corrected claim -- early electrum varied in its gold-to-silver ratio and could be manipulated; fungibility arrives with Kroisos's bimetallic reform, which is a better fact for this thesis than the one rev 1 had."
